{
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "outDir": "dist",
    "rootDir": "src",
    "types": ["node"],
    // apps/server is a private leaf app — nothing imports its .d.ts, so it emits
    // none. This overrides tsconfig.base.json:9's `"declaration": true`; it is
    // not a restatement of a default, and deleting it restores the inherited
    // `true` rather than leaving the flag unset.
    //
    // Declaration emit fails with TS2742 on every export whose type touches the
    // auth instance — `createAuth` and `type Auth` included: `betterAuth(...)`'s
    // inferred type reaches into @simplewebauthn/server and zod 4, both nested
    // under better-auth in the pnpm store and so unnameable from here. The
    // alternatives were worse: hoisting a second zod major into a package that
    // already depends on zod 3, or hand-writing a facade type that would
    // silently narrow the auth API later tasks build on.
    //
    // tsconfig.typecheck.json needs the same line for a reason that is not
    // obvious: `noEmit` does not switch the declaration-emit check off.
    "declaration": false
  },
  "include": ["src"]
}
